From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Apr 2026 12:22:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] include/string: remove constexpr from ~basic_string() for ARM
 GCC

ARM GCC does not emit an out-of-line definition for ~basic_string() when the destructor is marked constexpr, even through explicit template instantiation in string.cpp. This causes undefined reference errors at link time for locale.cpp and prebuilt libraries compiled at -O0.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 include/string | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/string b/include/string
index d282071abf..39c26e99f3 100644
--- a/include/string
+++ b/include/string
@@ -1201,7 +1201,11 @@ public:
   }
 #  endif // _LIBCPP_CXX03_LANG
 
+#if defined(__arm__) && !defined(__clang__)
+  inline ~basic_string() {
+#else
   inline _LIBCPP_CONSTEXPR_SINCE_CXX20 ~basic_string() {
+#endif
     __annotate_delete();
     if (__is_long())
       __alloc_traits::deallocate(__alloc_, __get_long_pointer(), __get_long_cap());
